  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1248 PM CDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nAnother mid to upper level trough will dig down along the west coast\nand keep the flow over Texas southwesterly for the latter half of\nthe week. The low level flow will continue to be southeasterly. \nPW values will increase from the southeast to northwest Wednesday \ninto Thursday. A shortwave trough in the southwesterly flow aloft \nwill interact with this moist airmass making showers and \nthunderstorms likely Thursday into early Friday. Models show PW \n1.75-2.00 inches over the western half of our CWA which could lead\nto locally heavy rain. WPC has this area in the slight (Level 2 \nof 4) risk for rainfall to exceed flash flood guidance Thursday. \nFriday evening the upper shortwave will move away to the \nnortheast, there still may be enough lift for isolated showers \nFriday night and Saturday. Dry weather will return for Saturday \nnight through Monday.\n\nWith cloudy skies and rain, temperatures will be cooler Thursday\nand Friday with highs mostly in the 70s. The weekend should be\nwarmer with less cloudiness and mainly dry weather.",
